    2. Pick 3-5 distinct k-values (anti-diagonal indices) spaced 4-8 apart, within [4,26].
    3. For each k, choose a b-center and segment length 2-9; compute b_min/b_max.
       Ensure consecutive k-pairs share overlapping b-ranges (overlap >= 2).
       Ensure all implied cells (r,c) = ((k+b)/2, (k-b)/2) are in-bounds and integer.
    4. Optionally split one segment into two non-overlapping pieces on the same k.
    5. Build output by placing segments and filling between consecutive active segments per b-line.
    6. Derive input by removing all fill (color 2) cells, restoring them to bg.
